From 873d341fdf08fe11798099d122c3a39b8cbd3190 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:03:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 087/100] wifi: xradio: Add XR829 support

The XR829 (SDIO 0a9e:2282) runs a newer firmware ("HT40" API) that uses
16-bit rate entries (modem type, bandwidth, flags, rate index) instead of
8-bit rate indices. Select it at runtime from the SDIO ID and convert from
the XR819 structures at the firmware boundary, so both chips keep sharing
the driver:
- firmware files xr829/{boot,fw,sdd}_xr829.bin, DPLL sync with the BT core
- start scan: scan type in the flags byte, rate entry
- template frames: 8-byte header with a rate entry
- receive indication: rate entry + 3 reserved bytes; map back to the old
  rate index, report 40 MHz / short GI
- join/start: 16-bit PHY mode word (modem, width, band, preamble) at 20 MHz
- TX: rate retry policies as up to 6 rate entries (same 12 bytes), TX
  request header in the new layout (policy index, first rate entry,
  data offset, PTA priority), built from the XR819 one
- TX confirm: rate entry and per-rate tries translated back to rate indices
- association mode MIB: 12-byte layout with PHY mode word, renumbered flags
- ARP reply template: 8-byte header
- override internal TX rate MIB: two rate entries

Also fixes, found while bringing the XR829 up:
- HT frames were flagged RX_ENC_HT in hdr->flag (= MMIC error) instead of
  hdr->encoding;
- the vendor skb cache reused an RX skb by resetting data, len and tail but
  not data_len, frags or the cloned state (skb_over_panic on a 520-byte
  frame); it is gone, every RX skb is freshly allocated;
- a WARN on debug-only message names;
- xradio_update_dpllctrl() checks the result of every AHB access and warns
  about a DPLL mismatch only once.

WPA2 (CCMP) station mode works: 29 Mbit/s RX and 12 Mbit/s TX in iperf3
at MCS 7, stable over 2 minutes.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
